.TH SDL_GetJoystickBall 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetJoystickBall \- Get the ball axis change since the last poll.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetJoystickBall(SDL_Joystick *joystick, int ball, int *dx, int *dy);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trackballs can only return relative motion since the last call to
.BR SDL_GetJoystickBall (),
these motion deltas are placed into
.BR dx
and
.BR dy \[char46]
.PP
Most joysticks do not have trackballs\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
the
.BR SDL_Joystick
to query\[char46]
.TP
.I ball
the ball index to query; ball indices start at index 0\[char46]
.TP
.I dx
stores the difference in the x axis position since the last poll\[char46]
.TP
.I dy
stores the difference in the y axis position since the last poll\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
